      {
        "id": 130025,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-03T04:38:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, keep in mind that you're spending the turn of an incapacitated hero and essentially nulling the draw of another hero if you plan on recycling this over and over. So if F6 Wraith goes first, she can take Legacy's Take Down from play (which will be used up and destroyed on his next turn) and send it to the top of his deck instead. Legacy will have to receive draw power from someone else to even use it next turn (otherwise it's every other turn, which isn't bad either). So that's essentially 2-3 heroes for the combo, not exactly an ideal situation because Legacy also won't get any new cards, since he'll constantly be using the same one. Granted, I had the Ennead in my setup, so Set's incapped power helped. But in a typical game you won't get to do this quite as easily unless you have Team Leader Tachyon. It CAN be overpowered, but in many cases it really isn't.</p><p>This combo can also be emulated by Bunker or Tachyon (One Player may take a card from their trash into their hand) or Tempest (<span>One Player may take an Ongoing card from their trash into their hand). The question remains, is it intended to work similarly to these? At the moment, it's open to interpretation.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
